        {
          "question": "q-161166",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\u27e8P,\\,Q,\\,R\u27e9$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\u222c}_{D}(\\frac{}{\u2202x}-Q\\frac{\u2202g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?",
